{"title":"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following expressions is equal to an odd integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340b9348105d6080078a9ea5e20a020fbf9e30f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3(5) + 1 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2(3 + 5) \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3(3 + 5) \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 3 + 5 + 1 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{3 + 5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"649\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can evaluate each of the answer choices until we get an odd integer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/1487a35385ea3650023ae86fc514a46bc1ec7615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(5) + 1 = 15 + 1 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is even, so A cannot be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd60b6deb154a96692ddf4ab734ca2166e229b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(3 + 5) = 2 \\times 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />. We got the same number, so B also cannot be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c299b364848df8356bb8a7d778ef25cdb8ffba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(3 + 5) = 3 \\times 8 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is even, so C cannot be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b00767835cbcfd97c148141b8d94c5c88ea2df79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 + 5}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is even, so E cannot be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b56859e1680b8c5f7eb40bb14cfb8f30d7b8772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, so D must be the answer.\n</p><p>Combining all of these or by seeing all of the answer choices are eliminated, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcb72c86262d5c626ee24192d8c6ac4aebffad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 3 + 5 + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28patterns.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(patterns)\">Solution 2 (patterns)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (patterns)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can eliminate answer choice A because an odd multiplied by an odd is an odd. Adding an odd to another odd number gives an even number, so the answer cannot be A.\n</p><p>We also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d899f75d45ace00b3fc81481ad33201c4980cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is even due to two odds being added together in both B and C. Since we have an even number multiplied by an integer in both answer choices, both B and C are even. Thus, we can eliminate both B and C.\n</p><p>With answer choice D, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d899f75d45ace00b3fc81481ad33201c4980cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is even because two odds added together gives an even number. However, adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> makes an odd number because an even number added to an odd number is odd.\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcb72c86262d5c626ee24192d8c6ac4aebffad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 3 + 5 + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8